Turning each block into a **dynamic key-value form** makes the whole system much cleaner and way more flexible—you aren't locked into rigid sub-blocks, and you can define whatever fields you need (like `Subject Outfit`, `Camera Angle`, `Analysis Focus`, etc.) on the fly.

Below is a **complete, ready-to-use interactive web app** in a single file. Just save it as `pipeline-builder.html` and double-click it to open in any browser (no server or install needed).

### What’s Built In
* **Top-Down Visual Blocks:** Click any block header to expand or collapse it. Reorder blocks up/down, swap block types, or insert new blocks anywhere in the flow.
* **Dynamic Form Rows Inside Every Block:** Add as many `[ Field Name ]` → `[ Content ]` rows as you want. Each row can also be toggled between:
  * **Form Field** (standard `Name: Content`, e.g., `Subject Outfit` → description)
  * **Photo Ref** (attaches a reference image preview + notes, e.g., `Subject Ref`, `Scene Ref`, `Analysis-Only Ref`)
  * **+ Positive** / **- Negative** (tags constraints clearly in the output)
* **Reusable Template Dropdown:** Pre-loaded with *Video Generation*, *Video Analyst*, and *Visual Analyst (2-Item Study)*—plus you can save your own modified pipelines as custom templates in your browser.
* **Live Markdown Output:** Updates in real time on the right as you type, with one-click **Copy** and **Download `.md`** buttons.

